{"cuisine/tamil-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/tamil-cuisine","n":"Tamil cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["South Indian cuisine","cuisine/south-indian-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in India","intro":[["Tamil cuisine is a generic term used to describe culinary practices among Tamil-speaking populations, originating from Southern India and neighboring Sri Lanka. It encompasses several distinct styles of cuisine or cooking repertoires, which can be divided at a basic level into Tamil cuisine of Southeastern India and Sri Lankan Tamil cuisine. The former is a fundamental part of what is now known as South Indian cuisine, with deep connections to other cooking styles of the southern Deccan. The latter is distinct to the Tamil-speaking populations natives to Ceylon, co-formed with other cooking styles unique to Sri Lanka (Sri Lankan cuisine). It shares significant culinary links with Southwestern India and Southeast Asia."],["Meats, along with rice, legumes, and lentils, are popular. Dairy products and tamarind are used to provide sour flavors. On special occasions, traditional Tamil dishes are served in a traditional manner, using banana leaves in place of utensils. After eating, the banana leaves are then used as a secondary food for cattle. A typical breakfast meal consists of idli or dosa with chutney, while lunch includes rice, sambar, curd, kuzhambu, and rasam."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"tamil-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tamil_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":1,"links":[["Ashoka Halwa","dish/ashoka-halwa"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"Cooking From Heart (Tamil Nadu)","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"cookingfromheart.com","note":"Tamil Nadu section of a South Indian vegetarian home cooking blog.","url":"https://cookingfromheart.com/category/tamilnadu-special/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Chitra's Food Book","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"chitrasfoodbook.com","note":"Chennai-based home cook's blog of everyday Tamil vegetarian recipes.","url":"https://chitrasfoodbook.com/?p=5163","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"Samaithu Paar (Cook and See)","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"S. Meenakshi Ammal","note":"Classic multi-volume guide to Tamil Brahmin vegetarian cooking, in print since the 1950s.","url":"","suggested":true},{"name":"Annapurni: Heritage Cuisine From Tamil Nadu","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Sabita Radhakrishna","note":"Heritage Tamil recipes and food lore, published by Roli Books.","url":"https://rolibooks.com/?p=12410","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Ghee","ingredient/ghee"],["Mung bean","ingredient/mung-bean"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["South Indian cuisine","cuisine/south-indian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Within Tamil cooking","count":1,"links":[["Chettinad cuisine","cuisine/chettinad-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/5d/Veg_Full_Meals_in_Tamil_Nadu.JPG/500px-Veg_Full_Meals_in_Tamil_Nadu.JPG","w":500,"h":511,"by":"KARTY JazZ","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Veg_Full_Meals_in_Tamil_Nadu.JPG"}},"ingredient/clam":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/clam","n":"Clam","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 4 dishes across 3 cuisines","intro":[["Clam is a common name for several species of bivalve mollusc. The word is often applied only to those that are deemed edible and live as infauna, spending most of their lives halfway buried in the sand of the sea floor or riverbeds. Clams have two shells of equal size connected by two adductor muscles and have a powerful burrowing foot. They live in both freshwater and marine environments; in salt water they prefer to burrow down into the mud. The turbidity of the water required varies with species and location; the greatest diversity of these is in North America."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-clam"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clam"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":3,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Clam chowder","dish/clam-chowder"],["Clam dip","dish/clam-dip"]]],["Cuisine of New England","cuisine/cuisine-of-new-england",[["Clam cake","dish/clam-cake"]]],["Portuguese cuisine","cuisine/portuguese-cuisine",[["Amêijoas à Bulhão Pato","dish/ameijoas-a-bulhao-pato"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Clams","ingredient/clams"],["Coriander","ingredient/coriander"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Peppercorn","ingredient/peppercorn"],["White wine","ingredient/white-wine"],["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Salt pork","ingredient/salt-pork"],["Cream cheese","ingredient/cream-cheese"],["Sour cream","ingredient/sour-cream"]]},{"h":"Mentioned in","links":[["Wampanoag foodways","cuisine/wampanoag-foodways"]]}]},"ingredient/bread-crumbs":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/bread-crumbs","n":"Bread crumbs","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 10 dishes across 10 cuisines","intro":[["Breadcrumbs are a culinary ingredient consisting of flour or crumbled bread of varying dryness, sometimes with seasonings added. They are used for a variety of purposes, including breading or crumbing foods before frying (such as breaded cutlets like tonkatsu and schnitzel), topping casseroles, stuffing poultry, thickening stews, and adding inexpensive bulk to soups, meatloaves, and similar foods."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-bread-crumbs"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bread_crumbs"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":10,"groups":[["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine",[["Chicken Kiev","dish/chicken-kiev"],["Pozharsky cutlet","dish/pozharsky-cutlet"]]],["Serbian cuisine","cuisine/serbian-cuisine",[["Karađorđeva šnicla","dish/kara-or-eva-snicla"],["Pljeskavica","dish/pljeskavica"]]],["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Brown Betty (dessert)","dish/brown-betty-dessert"]]],["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine",[["Scotch egg","dish/scotch-egg"]]],["Greek cuisine","cuisine/greek-cuisine",[["Taramasalata","dish/taramasalata"]]],["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine",[["Passatelli","dish/passatelli"]]],["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine",[["Curry bread","dish/curry-bread"]]],["Romanian cuisine","cuisine/romanian-cuisine",[["Taramasalata","dish/taramasalata"]]],["Turkish cuisine","cuisine/turkish-cuisine",[["Taramasalata","dish/taramasalata"]]],["Yoshoku","cuisine/yoshoku",[["Tonkatsu","dish/tonkatsu"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Breadcrumbs","ingredient/breadcrumbs"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Veal","ingredient/veal"],["Apple","ingredient/apple"],["Berry","ingredient/berry"],["Pear","ingredient/pear"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Zest","ingredient/zest"],["Japanese curry","ingredient/japanese-curry"],["Kaymak","ingredient/kaymak"],["Schnitzel","ingredient/schnitzel"],["Steak","ingredient/steak"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/e1/Breadcrumb.jpg/500px-Breadcrumb.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Yvwv","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Breadcrumb.jpg"}},"ingredient/parmesan":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/parmesan","n":"Parmesan","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 9 dishes across 6 cuisines","intro":[["Parmesan is an Italian hard, granular cheese produced from cow's milk and aged at least 12 months. It is a grana-type cheese, along with Grana Padano, the historic Granone Lodigiano, and others."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-parmesan"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parmesan"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":6,"groups":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine",[["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Cotoletta alla bolognese","dish/cotoletta-alla-bolognese"],["Lasagna","dish/lasagna"],["Passatelli","dish/passatelli"],["Spaghetti alla Nerano","dish/spaghetti-alla-nerano"]]],["Italian-American cuisine","cuisine/italian-american-cuisine",[["Fettuccine Alfredo","dish/fettuccine-alfredo"],["Tetrazzini","dish/tetrazzini"]]],["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"]]],["Louisiana Creole cuisine","cuisine/louisiana-creole-cuisine",[["Oysters Bienville","dish/oysters-bienville"]]],["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine",[["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"]]],["Sicilian cuisine","cuisine/sicilian-cuisine",[["Parmigiana","dish/parmigiana"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Basil","ingredient/basil"],["Extra virgin olive oil","ingredient/extra-virgin-olive-oil"],["Anchovy","ingredient/anchovy"],["Crouton","ingredient/crouton"],["Dijon mustard","ingredient/dijon-mustard"],["Lemon juice","ingredient/lemon-juice"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Parmigiano-Reggiano","ingredient/parmigiano-reggiano"],["Romaine lettuce","ingredient/romaine-lettuce"],["Worcestershire sauce","ingredient/worcestershire-sauce"],["Ham","ingredient/ham"],["Veal","ingredient/veal"],["Fettuccine","ingredient/fettuccine"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/d1/Parmigiano_Reggiano%2C_Italien%2C_Europ%C3%A4ische_Union.jpg/500px-Parmigiano_Reggiano%2C_Italien%2C_Europ%C3%A4ische_Union.jpg","w":500,"h":514,"by":"Naturpuur","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Parmigiano_Reggiano%2C_Italien%2C_Europ%C3%A4ische_Union.jpg"}},"ingredient/bell-peppers":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/bell-peppers","n":"Bell peppers","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 4 cuisines","intro":[["The bell pepper (also known as sweet pepper, paprika, pepper, capsicum  or, in some parts of the U.S. Midwest, mango) is the fruit of plants in the Grossum Group of the species Capsicum annuum. Cultivars of the plant produce fruits in different colors, including red, yellow, orange, green, white, and purple. Bell peppers are sometimes grouped with less pungent chili varieties as \"sweet peppers\". While they are botanically fruits—classified as berries—they are commonly used as a vegetable ingredient or side dish. Other varieties of the genus Capsicum are categorized as chili peppers when they are cultivated for their pungency, including some varieties of Capsicum annuum."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-bell-peppers"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bell_peppers"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":4,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Succotash","dish/succotash"]]],["Cali-Mex cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-california-latino-and-hispanic-influence",[["Celery Victor","dish/celery-victor"]]],["Cuisine of California","cuisine/cuisine-of-california",[["Celery Victor","dish/celery-victor"]]],["Wampanoag foodways","cuisine/wampanoag-foodways",[["Succotash","dish/succotash"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Celery","ingredient/celery"],["Romaine lettuce","ingredient/romaine-lettuce"],["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Edible salt","ingredient/edible-salt"],["Lima bean","ingredient/lima-bean"],["Sweet corn","ingredient/sweet-corn"],["Tomatoes","ingredient/tomatoes"],["Zea mays Saccharata Group","ingredient/zea-mays-saccharata-group"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/8/85/Green-Yellow-Red-Pepper-2009.jpg/500px-Green-Yellow-Red-Pepper-2009.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Kham Tran - www.khamtran.com","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Green-Yellow-Red-Pepper-2009.jpg"}},"ingredient/chhena":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/chhena","n":"Chhena","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Chhena ଛେନ୍ନା in Odia  or chhana (Bengali: [tʃʰana]) ছানা in Bengali, is a kind of acid-set cheese originating in the Indian subcontinent that is made from water buffalo or cow milk by adding food acids such as lemon juice and calcium lactate instead of rennet and straining out the whey."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-chhena"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chhena"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Bangladeshi cuisine","cuisine/bangladeshi-cuisine",[["Chhanamukhi","dish/chhanamukhi"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Maida (flour)","ingredient/maida-flour"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/aa/Chhena_Ball_-_Rasgulla_Preparation_-_Digha_-_East_Midnapore_-_2015-05-02_9555.JPG/500px-Chhena_Ball_-_Rasgulla_Preparation_-_Digha_-_East_Midnapore_-_2015-05-02_9555.JPG","w":500,"h":332,"by":"Biswarup Ganguly","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chhena_Ball_-_Rasgulla_Preparation_-_Digha_-_East_Midnapore_-_2015-05-02_9555.JPG"}},"dish/pudim-molotov":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/pudim-molotov","n":"Pudim Molotov","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Portuguese cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Pudim Molotov is a popular dessert in Portuguese cuisine. It is made with egg whites, sugar, and sometimes a touch of vanilla. The egg whites are whipped until stiff peaks form, then mixed with caramel sauce. The mixture is then baked in the oven, resulting in a light and fluffy dessert with a caramelized top."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pudim-molotov"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pudim_Molotov"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Portuguese cuisine","cuisine/portuguese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Egg white","ingredient/egg-white"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Food From Portugal","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"foodfromportugal.com","note":"Portuguese-run recipe site and video channel of traditional Portuguese dishes.","url":"https://www.foodfromportugal.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from Portuguese cuisine","links":[["Alheira","dish/alheira"],["Amêijoas à Bulhão Pato","dish/ameijoas-a-bulhao-pato"],["Arroz de marisco","dish/arroz-de-marisco"],["Bacalhau à Brás","dish/bacalhau-a-bras"],["Bacalhau à Gomes de Sá","dish/bacalhau-a-gomes-de-sa"],["Bacalhau à minhota","dish/bacalhau-a-minhota"],["Bacalhau à Narcisa","dish/bacalhau-a-narcisa"],["Bacalhau à Zé do Pipo","dish/bacalhau-a-ze-do-pipo"],["Bacalhau com natas","dish/bacalhau-com-natas"],["Batatas a murro","dish/batatas-a-murro"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Bolo de bolacha","dish/bolo-de-bolacha"],["Canja de galinha","dish/canja-de-galinha"],["Cocido","dish/cocido"],["Embutido","dish/embutido"],["Encharcada","dish/encharcada"],["Fartura","dish/fartura"],["Feijoada","dish/feijoada"],["Fios de ovos","dish/fios-de-ovos"],["Francesinha","dish/francesinha"],["Gazpacho","dish/gazpacho"],["Pão Alentejano","dish/pao-alentejano"],["Pão de Ló","dish/pao-de-lo"],["Pataniscas","dish/pataniscas"],["Polvo à lagareiro","dish/polvo-a-lagareiro"],["Prego (Portuguese sandwich)","dish/prego-portuguese-sandwich"],["Pudim Abade de Priscos","dish/pudi